  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed conversion into a large HMO (sui generis) would result in the loss of a dwelling with less than 130sq.m. floorspace (as originally constructed) which is suitable for occupation by families, as defined in Part A of Wandsworth Local Plan policy LP26. Accordingly, the development would result in harm to the provision of family housing within the borough and is contrary to Part A of LP26 and parts A.1 and A.4 of policy LP29 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023).",
    "Reason : 2 - By reason of its layout, the development would result in substandard residential accommodation for occupiers as the application has failed to demonstrate adequate level of daylight and outlook to the second floor front bedroom. Accordingly, the development is contrary to policies LP27 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023). ",
    "Reason : 3 - The site has a moderate public transport accessibility level (PTAL) of 3 which falls short of a PTAL of at least 4 as required by Policy LP29 A.4 which ensures shared facilities are located in well-connected locations. Accordingly, the development is contrary to policy LP29 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023).",
    "Reason : 4 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to work with the applicant in a positive and proactive manner and the Council has, as far as practicable, sought solutions to problems arising in relation to dealing with the planning application. We have made available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan consisting of the Core Strategy, Development Management Policies Document, Supplementary Planning documents and where appropriate the Site Specific Allocations Document as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the principle of the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal."
  ],
